# a-base-behind-a-moat — BACKLOG C5, and it is the THIRD of a triple.
#
# `a-base-nobody-builds.keys`, `a-base-the-player-builds.keys` and this
# file are the same file except for ONE token on one line:
#
#     paint off   →   nobody builds        falls at 130
#     paint on    →   a five-hex WALL      falls at 174   (`@M050`)
#     dig on      →   a five-hex TRENCH    ⚠⚠ does not fall at all
#
# Same ground, same core, same spawn, same wave list, same crew, same
# drive, same number of ticks spent before the wave — so every
# difference below is the trench's and can be nothing else
# (`plans/12` § B7's rule).
#
# ── ⚠⚠ What it costs, and the scenario says all three ────────────
#
# A wall is a barrier you may walk along; a trench is a CUT, and the
# reading is that it cuts EVERYTHING:
#
#   1. **the wave stops and never gets through** — water is not a
#      surface (`walk_ground: false`), so nothing on legs enters one,
#      and it has no HP, so there is nothing to chew.  The base does not
#      fall inside 300 ticks where the walled one fell at 174;
#   2. ⚠⚠ **and it earns NOTHING** — nothing that cannot reach you can
#      die, so no body drops, no heap is collected, and the wallet is
#      still on exactly its opening 200.  A wall's 174 ticks are ticks
#      the player was PAID for; these are not.  ⚠ That is `@M056`'s
#      jammer trade one mechanic over: time bought, income given up;
#   3. ⚠⚠ **and the player cannot get back over it.**  `docs/PLAYING.md`
#      calls boost *"the only way out of a base you have sealed"* and
#      that is true of WALLS, whose tops are walkable — a climb cannot
#      answer a surface question, so a 3.0 m boost does not cross a 1 m
#      ditch.  The drive east at the end goes nowhere.
#
# ⚠ **The crew dug themselves in**, which is the same rule from the
# inside: they stood on the line to work it, and a helper on a finished
# trench is on it for the run.

echo behind a moat: a trench drawn by driving, dug by the crew

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 12 -2
drag -3 -1 12 -1
drag -3 0 12 0
drag -3 1 12 1
drag -3 2 12 2
count painted 80 80

# The crew, sitting on the line the player is about to draw.
crew 5 -1
crew 5 1

# ── The dig ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
park 5 -2
dig on
drive 5 2
tick 6
count orders 5 5
dig off

# Park clear of the line so the trail is not rubbed out, and let the
# crew work.  A trench owes a wall's 10 s a hex — `build.loft`
# § BUILD_MOAT_UNITS chose that so the player's question is what it
# DOES rather than what it costs — so 50 helper-seconds over two
# helpers is 25 s, the same 45-tick window the wall version uses.
drive 0 0
tick 50
count orders 0 0
count painted 80 80
# ⚠⚠ The whole band, hex by hex — a barrier with ONE gap in it buys
# nothing at all (`plans/12` § B7 measured a gate at +1 tick), so
# *five* is the number that matters rather than *some*.
kind 5 -2 water
kind 5 -1 water
kind 5 0 water
kind 5 1 water
kind 5 2 water

# ⚠ The crew are in it.  They stood on the line to dig it and a helper
# on finished water cannot leave — the cost, stated where it happens.
helper 0 5 -1
helper 1 5 1


# ── The waves — identical to `an-undefended-base` ───────────────
wave 5
count alive 5 5

tick 22
wave 8
count alive 13 13

# ── The clock, and what it was bought with ──────────────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ **300 ticks and the base is still standing**, against 174 for the
# wall and 130 for nothing — and the wallet has not moved off its
# opening 200, because nothing that cannot reach you ever dies.
tick 300
ticks 375 385
wallet 200 200
count alive 13 13
# Stopped at the far bank, one hex east of the trench, attacking
# nothing: a moat has no HP, so the siege has nowhere to bite.
count targets 0 0

# ⚠⚠ And the player cannot follow them.  Point the vehicle at the
# spawn and give it ten ticks — thirty hexes of allowance — and it is
# still on the near side.
drive 11 0
tick 10
vehicle 4 0

snap c5_a_base_behind_a_moat
